# The incremental gate's backstop (ADR 0135, TESTING.md's Commands): one full
# `just pre-merge all` a day on `main`'s head, compared with the incremental
# runs of `just merge` (ci/gate-backstop.sh). It goes into the gate host's
# crontab (`crontab -e`), with GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT set to the main checkout.
# On a day the disk lacks room for its build it lists itself as skipped.
#
# It starts `origin/main`'s script, not the checkout's, which nothing
# fast-forwards; the script then runs the scripts of the commit it tests.
#
# A login shell gives it the host's PATH and build settings (~/.profile); cron
# adds what the shells the owner starts take from elsewhere. GOODFETCH_LAZYFS
# names the LazyFS build its re-stress needs for a `lazyfs::` test, outside
# every checkout since a gate clears its worktree's target/lazyfs/; without one
# on Linux the backstop lists itself as skipped before any step. Build one with
# `just lazyfs-build` and copy its target/lazyfs/bin/ there, again whenever
# test-support/lazyfs/sources.toml moves. SCCACHE_CLIENT_SIDE gives each compile
# its own cargo's jobs and nice level instead of the shared daemon's.
GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT=/Users/jb/Dev/goodfetch
GOODFETCH_LAZYFS=/Users/jb/.local/share/goodfetch/lazyfs/bin/lazyfs
SCCACHE_CLIENT_SIDE=1
37 3 * * * bash -lc 'cd "$GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT" && git fetch --quiet origin && script=$(git show origin/main:ci/gate-backstop.sh) && nice -n 10 bash -c "$script" gate-backstop origin/main'
